From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: write the TCL command of an extension descriptor frame after its TLV header

ath11k_hal_srng_src_get_next_entry() returns a u32 pointer, so adding
sizeof(struct hal_tlv_hdr) to it moves 16 bytes into the entry, not 4.
The extension descriptor send path did that, and wrote its TCL data
command 12 bytes past where the normal path (which adds to a void
pointer) and the TCL expect it. A TCL data ring entry is the 4 byte TLV
header and the 28 byte command (hal.c), so the TCL read for such a frame
the buffer address, cookie and descriptor type left in the entry by the
frame that used it before, followed by the first words of the new
command in place of its lengths and flags; the last 12 bytes of the
command went into the TLV header and buffer address of the next entry,
or past the end of the ring for its last entry.

That matches what the bench showed for extension descriptor frames: the
frame is not transmitted, its own cookie never completes, and the
firmware later releases a cookie of an older frame.

Write the command after the TLV header, as the normal path does.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
Index: backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
===================================================================
--- backports-7.2.orig/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -1145,6 +1145,8 @@ static int ath11k_dp_tx_ext(struct ath11
 	ti.data_len = sizeof(struct hal_tx_msdu_ext);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+		void *desc;
+
 		ti.desc_id = FIELD_PREP(DP_TX_DESC_ID_MAC_ID, ar->pdev_idx) |
 			     FIELD_PREP(DP_TX_DESC_ID_MSDU_ID,
 					ath11k_dp_tx_id_cookie(tx_ring, ids[i])) |
@@ -1154,9 +1156,10 @@ static int ath11k_dp_tx_ext(struct ath11
 		ti.paddr = tx_ring->ext_paddr +
 			   ath11k_dp_tx_ext_off(tx_ring, slots[i]);
 		tx_ring->id_addr[ids[i]] = ti.paddr;
-		ath11k_hal_tx_cmd_desc_setup(ab,
-					     ath11k_hal_srng_src_get_next_entry(ab, tcl_ring) +
-					     sizeof(struct hal_tlv_hdr), &ti);
+		/* the command follows the TLV header of the ring entry */
+		desc = ath11k_hal_srng_src_get_next_entry(ab, tcl_ring);
+		ath11k_hal_tx_cmd_desc_setup(ab, desc + sizeof(struct hal_tlv_hdr),
+					     &ti);
 	}
 
 	if (held_ring < 0) {
